{"title":"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Relay B Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_B_Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Replace <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> below with the number you receive.\n</p><p>The first number in a sequence is a positive integer, and then each number after that is one more than the previous number in the sequence. If the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /><sup>th</sup> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /><sup>th</sup> numbers add to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, what is the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /><sup>th</sup> number in the sequence?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_B_Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since each number after the first is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> more than the previous number, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/7/f17c9261f0accbf0c46932a94d524c0ddba03e48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{x} = x - 1 + a_{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"125\" height=\"17\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/7/ed7d0be4668e6bf3789c503a140955357aa6b8e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" /> represents the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /><sup>th</sup> number of the sequence. This means:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/1/9913ee21f0c179cd0cdd8f6d3927fa22c3488f36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{4} + a_{5} = 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"101\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d69b41c9d736609c0adce4cb463512cbb45abd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 - 1 + a_{1} + 5 - 1 + a_{1} = 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"226\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/b/37b084ce75e5caf4d5c8fc7026a2908653114ff5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a_{1} + 3 + 4 = 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"133\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/9/03902205a4f2e4c97bdf3cad8713c11d19f4bd4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a_{1} = 13 - 7 = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"135\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/0/9608abd1ce19cfdd70b20026fe29800f3d6d642e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{1} = \\frac{6}{2} = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"90\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/3/3e30a348ae7344c2bb810eef3144bada09070428.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{m} = m - 1 + 3 = m + 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"198\" height=\"17\" /> for some integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>From <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_B_Problem_1\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Relay B Problem 1\">player 1</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/0/0009dc22fa07f7cca840e7ad45abf9456c41c684.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" />. This means that the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /><sup>th</sup> number in the sequence would be the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /><sup>th</sup> number of the sequence, so the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /><sup>th</sup> number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/c/b1c2ace9c57188f2b5b25501b78646ba8f3c4bbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8 + 2 = \\boxed{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"96\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC\">2025 CEMC TUC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_B_Problem_1\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Relay B Problem 1\">Relay B Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_B_Problem_3\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Relay B Problem 3\">Relay B Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2025 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_